    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d623">

                <pb facs="0740" n="1574" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1574"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 656.119/892</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Laughlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-11-25">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 25, 1918</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received 6.26 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4026. War Trade Board [from Sheldon]:</p>
                <p>No. 1941. Dutch agreement was signed tonight. Such alterations as were made in
                    text sent you in my 1874, Embassy’s 3727, November 14,<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d623-f1"/> will be cabled you tomorrow. Of course the general
                    embargo for all articles on the ration list is automatically lifted.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Laughlin</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
